  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the interaction with NCI-H526 through multiple pathways, with the P2X purinoceptor 1 serving as a common target across three distinct evidence chains. The first two paths link doxorubicin to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is then targeted by palmarumycin CP18 and Mollicellin N, respectively, both of which have a known effect on NCI-H526. The third path connects doxorubicin to LC4-1, which is targeted by a complex compound with a specific molecular structure that also affects NCI-H526. These findings suggest that doxorubicin may exert its effects on NCI-H526 through diverse molecular mechanisms, potentially involving purinoceptor modulation or complex compound interactions. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between doxorubicin and NCI-H526, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and pathways underscores the complexity of the relationship, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
